NNAAMMEE
       EVP_RAND-SEED-SRC - The randomness seed source EVP_RAND implementation

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Support for deterministic random number generator seeding through the
       EEVVPP__RRAANNDD API.

       The seed sources used are specified at the time OpenSSL is configured
       for building using the ----wwiitthh--rraanndd--sseeeedd== option.  By default, operating
       system randomness sources are used.

   IIddeennttiittyy
       "SEED‐SRC" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
       EEVVPP__RRAANNDD__ffeettcchh(()) function.

   SSuuppppoorrtteedd ppaarraammeetteerrss
       The supported parameters are:

       "state" (OOSSSSLL__RRAANNDD__PPAARRAAMM__SSTTAATTEE) <integer>
       "strength" (OOSSSSLL__RRAANNDD__PPAARRAAMM__SSTTRREENNGGTTHH) <unsigned integer>
       "max_request" (OOSSSSLL__RRAANNDD__PPAARRAAMM__MMAAXX__RREEQQUUEESSTT) <unsigned integer>
           These parameters work as described in "PARAMETERS" in EEVVPP__RRAANNDD(3).

NNOOTTEESS
       A context for the seed source can be obtained by calling:

        EVP_RAND *rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "SEED-SRC", NULL);
        EVP_RAND_CTX *rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand);

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
        EVP_RAND *rand;
        EVP_RAND_CTX *seed, *rctx;
        unsigned char bytes[100];
        OSSL_PARAM params[2], *p = params;
        unsigned int strength = 128;

        /* Create a seed source */
        rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "SEED-SRC", NULL);
        seed = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, NULL);
        EVP_RAND_free(rand);

        /* Feed this into a DRBG */
        rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "CTR-DRBG", NULL);
        rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, seed);
        EVP_RAND_free(rand);

        /* Configure the DRBG */
        *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_CIPHER,
                                                SN_aes_256_ctr, 0);
        *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
        EVP_RAND_instantiate(rctx, strength, 0, NULL, 0, params);

        EVP_RAND_generate(rctx, bytes, sizeof(bytes), strength, 0, NULL, 0);

        EVP_RAND_CTX_free(rctx);
        EVP_RAND_CTX_free(seed);

